{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואכלוהו", :translit "v'akhluhu", :gloss "and [they] shall eat it"} {:he "ואכלוהו אויביכם", :translit "v'akhluhu oyveikhem", :gloss "and your enemies shall eat it"} {:he "ואכלוהו במקום קדוש", :translit "v'akhluhu bimkom kadosh", :gloss "and you shall eat it in a holy place"} {:he "ואכלוהו ויכלוהו", :translit "v'akhluhu vikhluhu", :gloss "and [they] shall eat it and consume it"} {:he "ואכלוהו במקום קדוש שתשמרו מצותי ותשארו בארץ במקום קדוש", :translit "v'akhluhu bimkom kadosh shetishmeru mitzvotai v'tisha'aru ba'aretz bimkom kadosh", :gloss "and you shall eat it in a holy place, that you would keep My commandments and remain in the land in a holy place"} {:he "ואכלוהו ויכלוהו", :translit "v'akhluhu vikhluhu", :gloss "and it shall be eaten and consumed"} {:he "ואת נוהו השמו", :translit "v'et naveihu hashimu", :gloss "and your habitation shall be made desolate"} {:he "ואכלוהו אוביכם", :translit "v'akhluhu oyveikhem", :gloss "and your enemies shall eat it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ואכלוהו אויביכם" "ואכלוהו במקום קדוש" "ואכלוהו ויכלוהו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Three identical phrase-roots read as a progression: intended blessing turned to curse through Israel's failure to keep the commandments."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'ואכלוהו במקום קדוש' appears in Leviticus 10:13 and 14:12 in contexts of priestly consumption in holiness. The tokhekhah (rebuke) of Leviticus 26:14-43 warns that if Israel fails to keep the commandments, the land will be ravaged by enemies and laid desolate. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the threefold occurrence of 'ואכלוהו' as a narrative arc: the intended 'eating in a holy place' is reversed into 'enemies shall eat it' because Israel did not keep the commandments, consistent with the tokhekhah's stated condition 'ואם לא תשמעו לי ולא עשיתם את כל המצות האלה' (Leviticus 26:14-16).", :sources ["Leviticus 10:13" "Leviticus 14:12" "Leviticus 26:14-16" "Leviticus 26:32"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ואכלוהו אויביכם" "ואכלוהו במקום קדוש" "ואכלוהו ויכלוהו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואכלוהו אויביכם", :refs ["Leviticus 26:16"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ואכלוהו במקום קדוש", :refs ["Leviticus 24:9"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ואכלוהו ויכלוהו", :refs ["Jeremiah 10:25"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Three identical phrase-roots read as a progression: intended blessing turned to curse through Israel's failure to keep the commandments.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:12.014565586Z", :model "glm-5.2"}